{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OcneanuTrace","lean:module:QOU.Mass.HeckeStokesEigenvalues","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.shadow_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.shadow_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L239-L240","doc":"The model's shadow ring is not zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.laurentModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.laurentModel","kind":"instance","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L230-L237","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.evalOne_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.evalOne_T","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L227-L228","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.evalOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.evalOne","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L224-L225","doc":"Evaluation at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.tower","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L206-L222","doc":"The rank-one Markov-trace tower over `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.qU_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.qU_inv","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L204-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.qU_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.qU_val","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L202-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.qU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.qU","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L198-L200","doc":"The deformation parameter `q = T 1`, a unit with inverse `T (-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.LaurentModel.R","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L195-L196","doc":"The Laurent ring `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_coxeter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_coxeter","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L171-L178","doc":"**Coxeter presentation.** The three relations of `S_n` on the shadow generators, bundled:\ninvolution, braid, far commutation. This is the content of \"the classical shadow is a\npermutation representation\", which the probe measured as `S₃` at `n = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L167-L169","doc":"Each shadow generator is a unit, its own inverse (a transposition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_far_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_far_comm","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L160-L165","doc":"The shadow satisfies far commutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_braid","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L153-L158","doc":"The shadow satisfies the braid relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.subsingleton_of_isUnit_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.subsingleton_of_isUnit_h","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L133-L144","doc":"**Why the base must be a ring and not a field.** If `q − q⁻¹` is a unit of `R` (for instance\n`R` a field and `q ≠ ±1`), then `ε` sends it both to a unit and, since `ε(q) = ε(q⁻¹) = 1`, to `0`,\nso the shadow ring is zero. A tower at one fixed value of `q` cannot carry the `q = 1` shadow; the\nparameter has to vary, as it does over `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (`LaurentModel.laurentModel`). This is the\ndefect of the earlier field-based form of this class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_hecke_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_hecke_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L126-L131","doc":"The classical shadow satisfies the Hecke quadratic at `q = 1`: `(X − 1)(X + 1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_involution","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L120-L124","doc":"**The shadow is an involution (derived).** Push the Hecke quadratic through `ε`: the\n`h • g` term dies (`shadow_kills_h`), leaving `ε(g)² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_kills_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_kills_h","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L113-L118","doc":"**The shadow forgets exactly the deformation.** `ε((q − q⁻¹) • g) = 0`: the classical target\nsees `h = 0`, i.e. the `q = 1` specialisation. What Step 2 leaves stipulated is therefore the\ndeformation `1 ↦ q` alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_at_one_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_at_one_inv","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L107-L111","doc":"The shadow also sends `q⁻¹` to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.hecke_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.hecke_factor","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L90-L105","doc":"**The two Stokes/Hecke eigenvalues are a consequence.** Every generator factors as\n`(g − q)(g + q⁻¹) = 0` in `A` — the algebra behind `stokes_curvature_factors`, now derived from\nthe monodromy hypothesis instead of stipulated as a curvature. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.shadow_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The shadow is the specialisation `q ↦ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.far_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.far_comm","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Far commutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.braid","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The braid relation between neighbours. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.quad","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L77-L77","doc":"The Hecke quadratic on every generator, with `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy","kind":"class","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/HeckeMonodromy.lean#L67-L83","doc":"**Conjecture (Step 2 as monodromy).** For a Markov-trace tower `T : MarkovTrace R A` over a\ncommutative ring `R`, with generators `T.g i`, a unit `q : Rˣ`, and a ring map `ε : A →+* B`: the\ngenerators are the monodromies of the substrate connection around the branch points of the colour\ncubic, so they satisfy the Hecke quadratic with `h = q − q⁻¹` and the braid and far-commutation\nrelations of the braid group; and `ε` lies over the specialisation `q ↦ 1`, which makes each shadow\ngenerator an involution (the Picard–Lefschetz transposition on the two colliding roots,\n`shadow_involution`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:hecke-monodromy-step-two","label":"conj:hecke-monodromy-step-two","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-monodromy-step-two.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}